    // Fuzzed parameter is the caller address that will attempt to airDrop.
    // General rule to check: for ANY caller address `who`, if they start with balance 0,
    // the reference allows them to call airDrop and their balance becomes 20.
    // The mutant inverts the hasNoBalance check and will block such callers.
    function testFuzz_property(address who) public {
        // avoid the zero address to keep domain sensible (still wide)
        vm.assume(who != address(0));

        // Ensure 'who' has zero initial tokenBalance (the reference requires caller to have zero)
        // The mapping defaults to 0, but make sure no prior interactions happened: operate directly.

        // Make the call as `who` and capture whether it succeeded (no revert) for observation.
        bool ok;
        vm.startPrank(who);
        try c.airDrop() {
            ok = true;
        } catch {
            ok = false;
        }
        vm.stopPrank();

        // The universal property we assert (single assertTrue):
